WEBVTT

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.200
BABY DORY: Hi. I'm Dory.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.240
I suffer from
short-term remembory loss.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.480
-Yes!
-That's exactly what you say!

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.400
Okay, okay.
We'll pretend to be the other kids now.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.560
-(JENNY INHALES DEEPLY)
-(CHARLIE CLEARS THROAT)

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.160
-(GASPS) Hi, Dory!
-Ahoy there!

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:07.600
-(LAUGHING)
-Do you want to play hide-and-seek?

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:09.520
Okay. I love-- Okay.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.000
We'll hide
and you count and come find us.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:12.880
Okay, Daddy.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.000
No, not Daddy. I'm the nice fish
who wants to be your friend, okay?

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.320
-Okay, Daddy.
-No.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:22.320
-I'm hiding.
-Now count to ten.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.160
One, two, three...

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.440
Um, four...

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.600
Um...

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:33.840
I like sand. Sand is squishy.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:37.200
-(FISH LAUGHING PLAYFULLY)
-Mommy, can I go play with them?

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.720
-Dory. Dory. Dory, honey.
-Dory. Kelpcake.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.560
Undertow, sweetie.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.280
Remember, honey, we have to
stay away from the undertow.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.600
Okay, sweetheart,
what about that rhyme we learned?

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.600
♪ We see the undertow and we say...

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:51.640
♪ Let's go

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:56.880
No. It's, "Heck no."
Okay? Let's try it again.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.760
♪ We see the undertow and we say...

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.800
♪ There's the undertow!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.560
♪ There's the undertow
There is the undertow

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:08.760
♪ Hey, you found the undertow
And we see the undertow ♪

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.200
-Did I forget again?
-No, no. No.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.120
-No, sweetie. Don't worry about it.
-No biggie, kelpcake.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.640
What if I forget you?
(GASPS) Would you ever forget me?

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:24.760
-(GASPS)
-Oh, kelpcake, no.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:29.720
We will never forget you, Dory.
And we know you'll never forget us.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.480
BABY DORY: Hello?

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:14.960
Hello!

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.640
-Did you hear that?
-What's that? Hear what?

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.360
-Stan, I just heard someone say hello.
-I didn't hear anybody say hello.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:24.160
I don't know, Stan.
I just heard someone say hello.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:28.440
There's a lot of fish here.
Anybody could have just said hello.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:29.800
-BABY DORY: Hello?
-There.

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:31.280
-STAN: Where?
-There. There. Right there.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.560
-Where am I looking?
-There!

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.600
-Oh.
-Hello!

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:37.520
-BABY DORY: Hello?
-Oh my goodness, it's a child!

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.880
-STAN: Hi, kid. Over here. Hello?
-Hello? Hi.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.720
Hi. I'm Dory. Can you please help me?

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.640
Hi, Dory. Are you lost?

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.280
-Yeah, where are your parents?
-Um...

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.200
I can't remember.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.080
-Oh.
-Well we'll look around.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:56.040
Are any of these fish your parents?

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:05.000
Hi, I'm Dory. Can you please help me?

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:06.480
-What?
-Um...

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:08.080
(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.480
-Honey, you just said that.
-Mmm.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.040
-I did?
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:18.080
I'm sorry. I suffer from
short-term remembory loss.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:21.000
-Oh, how awful.
-Short-term memory loss?

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.920
Okay, you wait here for one second.
Okay, sweetie pie?

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.520
-Stan. Stan. Stan.
-What? What?

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.200
What do we do? The poor thing is lost!

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.360
-What do you want me to do?
-We have to do something.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:32.360
-She can't remember a thing!
-She could come from anywhere.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:37.040
Wow, you are no help today.
Dory? Sweetie? How about we--

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.120
She's gone.
Well, that's not good. Hey, Dory!

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.400
-Dory!
-Dory!

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:47.400
I'm Dory. I lost my family.
Can you help me?

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:53.280
I'm Dory. I suffer from
short-term memory-- (GASPS)

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:03.040
♪ Just keep swimming
Just keep swimming

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.320
♪ Just keep swimming
Swimming What do we do? ♪

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:16.520
Hi. I lost my family. Can you help me?

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.080
Where did you see them last?

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:22.200
Well, uh, funny story, but I forgot.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:24.240
Oh, sweetie,
do you want to come swim with us?

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.360
That is the nicest offer
I've gotten all day.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:29.400
I think. Uh, I can't remember.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.400
Anyhoo, thanks, (CHUCKLES)
but I'm looking for someone.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:34.680
(SIGHS)

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:37.280
Oh. Can't remember. Can't remember.
Can't remember.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.560
-Hi! I'm Dory.
-(FISH GASP)

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:42.920
Was it something I said?

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:46.080
Kidding. Okay, you're not coming back.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.960
I was looking for something and I--
Okay, get it. Date night. Have fun.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:54.200
Well, I hope you find whatever it is
you're looking for.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:57.040
You and me both.
Any idea what that was?

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:58.600
I'm sorry.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:05:59.640
I'm sorry.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:05.760
Okay. Guess we'll hang out another
time. Don't be a stranger, Stranger.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:12.280
Huh?

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:15.880
MARLIN: A white boat!
They took my son!

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:18.840
-My son! Help me! Please!
-(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:19.960
-Watch out!
-(BOTH SCREAMING)

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.440
(GROANING)

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:25.400
Oh! Oh, sorry! Are you okay?

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:27.320
-He's gone. He's gone.
-There, there.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:28.520
-No, he's gone.
-It's all right.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:29.960
-He's gone.
-It'll be okay.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.200
No, no, they took him away.
I have to find the boat.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.360
A boat? Hey, I've seen a boat!

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:36.560
-You have?
-Uh-huh.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:38.320
It went this way! Follow me!

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:41.480
Thank you! Thank you.
Thank you so much!

